// Title: UAC Bypass Using ChangePK and SLUI
// Sigma ID: 503d581c-7df0-4bbe-b9be-5840c0ecc1fc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2024-12-01
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects an UAC bypass that uses changepk.exe and slui.exe (UACMe 61)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mattharr0ey.medium.com/privilege-escalation-uac-bypass-in-changepk-c40b92818d1b
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
//   - https://medium.com/falconforce/falconfriday-detecting-uac-bypasses-0xff16-86c2a9107abf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_changepk_slui.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\changepk.exe" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\slui.exe" and (ProcessIntegrityLevel in~ ("High", "System", "S-1-16-16384", "S-1-16-12288"))
